# Milestone: M3
# Covers: an allocation-heavy strand sets vm->gc_pending (debt > threshold);
#         urbi_gc_slice is invoked at the next dispatch-loop safepoint of any
#         strand; GC slice runs and clears the pending flag (row 12 §4.4 —
#         gc_pending safepoint hook in dispatch_loop_until_yield).
#
# Activated: v0.10.7 W7 — GC-managed cell types (UObject) allocatable from
# REPL since M4/M6.  Object.new() loops 5000 iterations without OOM;
# the loop completes and GC slice has run multiple times.
# Old label: M4 (no GC-managed cell allocations available from REPL at M3)
#
# Note: uses Object.new() (available since M6 stdlib) in a while loop.
# String.new("x") is not available (arity mismatch); Object.new() is the
# GC-managed cell type used here.  Loop terminates at i=5000 confirming
# gc_pending does not OOM the process.

var i = 0; while (i < 5000) { var s = Object.new(); s = nil; i = i + 1 }; i
[00000000] 5000
